# Run artifacts. What stays out is the bulk and the machine-local scratch; what stays in
# is the reasoning -- the .txt summaries and the sampled menu frames a campaign was
# actually decided on.

# Ignored by TYPE, not by location. The previous rule here was `videos/`, which was
# correct for the layout it was written against and silently stopped covering anything
# when the study runners began writing the mp4 next to the JSONs inside each arm
# directory instead. That drift went unnoticed until `hard_study/` and `sync_study/`
# turned out to be carrying 2.2 GB of untracked video between them. A rule that names a
# place expires when the place moves; one that names the artifact does not.
*.mp4
*.json
*.log
ladder_progress.log

# Old layout, still on disk. Kept as a rule so an archived tree does not reappear.
videos/
logs/

# Machine-local process scratch. A .pid is not merely useless once committed, it is
# actively wrong: it names a process id on ONE machine, and anything that reads it
# elsewhere is signalling whatever unrelated process now holds that number.
*.pid
*.started

# Kept, deliberately: the conclusions, and the evidence small enough to travel with them.
# `comparison.txt` and `analysis.txt` are what a campaign is read from a year later --
# the JSONs behind them are re-derivable in kind but not in value, and are the one thing
# here worth revisiting if the repo ever wants its raw numbers under version control.
!.gitignore
!*.txt
!*.jpg
